## Reproduced structural defect

The field-authoritative correspondence itself selects the intended same-column axial source mapping; the competing diagonal mapping remains `37.9670987281°` from the axial field and must not be restored.

The new failure is downstream in `periodic_chart_segment()`. Coverage clipping uses `1e-10` tolerance but emitted barycentric interval endpoints retain the tolerance-expanded values instead of being canonicalized onto the exact source simplex. At cylinder cell 29 two sides that geometrically share a source vertex acquire microscopic source-face-30 tails near `-1e-10`. The unchanged strict shared-endpoint/self-intersection predicate therefore sees overlap beyond the exact endpoint and correctly rejects the emitted chart.

Independent reconstruction from the immutable packaged source/fixture reproduces the first rejection at **cell 29**, matching runtime diagnostics.

The next fix is producer endpoint canonicalization, **not validator tolerance relaxation**.

